<title>RUSSIA: Russian non-CIS Jan-May oil exports edge up yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Russian non-CIS Jan-May oil exports edge up yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian oil exports in January-May outside  the Commonwealth of Independent States, or CIS, rose 1.9 percent year-on-year  to 42.93 million tonnes (2.06 million barrels per day), Fuel and Energy  Ministry data showed Friday.</p>
<p>A report from the ministry's commercial information service InfoTEK  said total crude exports, including to CIS countries, were down 1.6  percent in the first five months of 1997 to 51.22 million tonnes (2.46  million bpd).</p>
<p>The Black Sea port of Novorossiisk dominated exports in the first  five months, accounting for 24 percent of total deliveries in the  first five months.</p>
